              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "egrolman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Incredibly easy to make and very tasty. I added bananas and served it topped with Cool Whip Lite. Nice summer recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Michele Stern Galindo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for a Memorial Day bar-b-que potluck, and it was a hit! I am not very good with desserts, so the easier and simpler the better. I made this pretty much along the lines of the recipe, but I used about 1/2 cup blueberries and kiwi, each. I used about 2 cups of strawberries. I also used angel food cake and French vanilla yogurt. I was hesitant with the yogurt - not everyone likes this. However, combined with the angel food cake, which can be super sweet, the yogurt tasted more like pudding. Minimal ingredients, easy, refreshing, tasty - a perfect summer dessert!",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-07T01:22:07.577Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "amanda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very yummy, although I did alter it a bit. I made it with half yogurt and half Cool Whip, added a tsp. almond extract and added kiwi and some pineapple because I had it on hand.",
